This windows-legacy branch preserves the earlier Mole/digger command contract.
The MIT Bash/Go fork is caezium/burrow-digger, formerly named burrow-engine,
based on tw93/Mole at 9daf936ea5fd1a0648579434c76000cd9cfa1253 (V1.42.0).
Its original MIT notice is retained in THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.md. Burrow's Windows
app supplies a separately vendored MIT Mole PowerShell runtime with its own
LICENSE and pinned provenance; it exposes the legacy burrow-engine.cmd name.

The current caezium/burrow-engine repository is a separate FSL-1.1-ALv2 Rust
engine. This branch does not replace its legacy adapter with that runtime.

Optional separate-process tools:
  - fclones — MIT — https://github.com/pkolaczk/fclones
  - czkawka_core / czkawka_cli — MIT — https://github.com/qarmin/czkawka
    The GPL Krokiet/Cedinia frontends are not incorporated.
  - Bulk Crap Uninstaller — Apache-2.0 —
    https://github.com/Klocman/Bulk-Crap-Uninstaller

No copyleft source is incorporated into this CLI. Dependency license metadata
is checked in CI; the provenance of adapted ideas is recorded in PROVENANCE.md.
